\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 III. System Architecture and Integration
\fs28 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 The program is constructed using a Modular Layered Architecture to decouple the physical hardware layers from the application logic and diagnostic services.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa319\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 \strokec2 1. Initialization Phase (setup)
\fs24 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Hardware Baseline: Initializes the Hardware Serial UART at 115,200 baud for local console output.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Logging Launch: 
\fs26 Debug::begin()
\fs24  is called immediately to initialize the FreeRTOS queue and spawn the 
\fs26 DebugTask
\fs24 .\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Network Establishment: 
\fs26 WiFiManager::begin()
\fs24  attempts to connect to the local network using credentials stored in NVM.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Sequential Blocking: 
\fs26 WiFiManager::waitForClient()
\fs24  is called within 
\fs26 setup()
\fs24 . This intentionally pauses the program execution until a TCP client (e.g., JMRI) is successfully connected, ensuring the bridge is ready before the main loop begins.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Multicore Tasking: The 
\fs26 communicationTask
\fs24  is pinned to Core 0 to handle network I/O, while the main loop is reserved for LocoNet hardware timing on Core 1.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa319\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 2. Execution Loop (loop)
\fs24 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Timing Criticality: The 
\fs26 loop()
\fs24  function is dedicated to 
\fs26 lnStream.process()
\fs24 , ensuring that LocoNet bit-timings are maintained without interruption.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Asynchronous Flow: Diagnostic messages are generated via 
\fs26 LOG_DEBUG
\fs24  and pushed to a queue. The 
\fs26 DebugTask 
\fs24 consumes this queue at the lowest possible priority (
\fs26 tskIDLE_PRIORITY
\fs24 ), meaning logs are only transmitted when the CPU has idle cycles, preventing them from delaying critical packets.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
